  <h2 id="not-doctor">Why this is not an MBBS or clinical path</h2>

  <p>
    This is the single most common confusion around this keyword, so it gets its own section instead of a footnote.
  </p>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      A biotechnology degree gives you deep science knowledge applied to medicine - not a licence to practise it. If patient-facing clinical work, diagnosis, or prescribing is what you actually want, this is the wrong article; look at MBBS, BDS, nursing, or pharmacy instead.
    </p>
    <p>
      If what you actually want is to work on the science, data, quality, or regulatory side of medicine without becoming a clinician, keep reading - that is exactly what this field offers, and it is a genuinely strong option in its own right.
    </p>
  </div>

